  "title": "Finite-Time Convergence and Regret Guarantees for Neural Reinforcement Learning in POMDPs",
  "summary": "This paper investigates the finite-time convergence and regret guarantees for neural reinforcement learning in partially observable Markov Decision Processes (POMDPs), addressing the computational challenges posed by the curse of long-range dependence and proposing a framework with nonlinear neural value function approximation to achieve finite-time sublinear regret.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "This paper establishes a new finite-state MDP point-wise approximation error bound, laying the foundation for our RL algorithm design and analysis in POMDPs.",
